# Every text file is checked out with LF endings on every system. Git on a Windows runner
# has core.autocrlf=true, which would otherwise give the snapshots in
# crates/pitboard/tests/snapshots and every file a test reads with include_str! CRLF endings,
# and fail them there alone. Windows' own command scripts keep the CRLF that cmd.exe expects.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
